          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": "{}\n### Summary of Changes\n\nFixed the resource leak in shell completion by ensuring contexts created during completion are properly managed through Python's context manager protocol:\n\n1. **`src/click/shell_completion.py`**:\n   - Wrapped top-level context creation in [`_resolve_context`](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-ntw4gvm9/repo/src/click/shell_completion.py#L532) using `with cli.make_context(...) as ctx:`.\n   - Wrapped sub-context creation for non-chained groups using `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_ctx:`.\n   - Wrapped sub-context creation for chained groups using `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_sub_ctx:`.\n\nThis ensures file handles and resources registered via `Context.call_on_close` and `Context.with_resource` are automatically closed and cleaned up during completion execution, eliminating unclosed file `ResourceWarning`s.\n",
          "error": null
        }
